@@ -30,6 +31,14 @@ The source root must be the normal base stage. The finished release root
 rewrites the UI manifest; accepting that later stage needs a separate matching
 receipt contract, rather than ignoring a manifest mismatch.
 
+The cursor and Labwc inputs pass the same verifiers as the normal finished
+release. Their binaries, licenses and Labwc corresponding source are selected
+through a read-only logical overlay, without changing or duplicating the base
+root. They get the normal release's root ownership and modes in the subset.
+`component_inputs` records the verified receipts; `component_overrides` records
+their selected bytes and any replaced base file's hash separately. Source
+selection, component replacements and generated UI overrides remain distinct.
+
 ## Selection and limits
 
 The initial profile keeps Labwc, Quickshell, the normal keyboard and UI,
@@ -39,6 +48,21 @@ CA certificates and D-Bus/input data. Script interpreters and the Python
 standard library are included when needed. Optional GTK platform themes and
 non-SQLite Qt SQL backends are outside this session.
 
+The profile retains the normal default Jade Horse theme and the imported
+QtQuick, QtQml, Qt and Quickshell module families. Other installed themes,
+KDE/Dolphin/designer plugins, optional Qt multimedia/3D QML, Python Tk and
+Python development configuration are not part of this Qt desktop profile.
+
+The compact profile adds an explicit normal user menu extension that hides
+the installed-system menu entries and offers Terminal and Keyboard. The bar
+contains Menu, Clock and Keyboard; unavailable service panels, idle locking
+and power actions are disabled. Labwc retains compositor window actions,
+Foot and menu bindings; Home opens the menu. Browser/file-manager launchers
+are not exposed in this profile. These generated configuration overrides have
+separate original/generated hashes in `profile_overrides`; the verified normal
+component and its default menu remain unchanged. Source-selection hashes are
+not presented as hashes of overridden output files.
+
 This is an explicit first profile, not proof of every runtime `dlopen`, QML
 import, helper or optional panel dependency. Missing files/dependencies and
 limits refuse a build. Large applications such as browsers are not included.
